erence/store-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"an install or update: `path`, `release`, `fetched`, `reused`, `kept`, `changed`;"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"a refresh: `timestamp`, `files`, `bytes`; a repair: `path`, `health`, `fetched`; `remove`: `path`, `release`;"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#store","content":"`find` and `locate`: one row per place and pack that covers it: `id`, `name`, `lat`, `lon`, `countries`, then the pack's `pack`, `release`, `download`, `disk` and `state`, null for a place no pack in the catalog covers."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-33","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"Sets up a store at `root` and opens it: the metadata mirrors `repo` and asset mirrors `assets` (comma-separated URLs), and `trusted_root`, the catalog's root metadata, which becomes its trust anchor once it verifies by itself. A store set up before is set up again with these."},"1679":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::Refused` if the root does not verify or the store cannot be written."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#create","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1681":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#open","content":"Opens the store at `root`, finishing or undoing an install a crash cut short."},"1682"