url":"/docs/reference/store#engine","content":"**Blocks.** While a job of this store runs, and on the disk: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-61","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#refresh","content":"Refreshes the catalog for the countries (comma-separated ISO codes) and every country installed. Fails with `ErrorCode::Network` or `ErrorCode::Refused`."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-62","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install","content":"Installs the packs with `options`, dependencies first, refreshing the catalog for their countries. Cancelled, it leaves the store as it was; the packs installed before the one cut stay installed."},"1708":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-63","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` for an unknown component or language tag, more than 8 languages, or an outline level above 255; the job's own errors are the job's."},"1709":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-64","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install_pass","content":"One pass of an install whose bytes a platform's own download service fetches, for downloads that must go on while the app is suspended. The pass reads each asset's ranges from files under `dir`, checks every byte as from any host, and its result lists what is still missing, one row per range: `pack`, `urls` (the asset on each mirror, one per line), `length` (the asset's), `start` and `end` (the range, end exclusive) and `file`, where to save those bytes. Fetch every listed range (an HTTP `Range` request for `bytes=start-(end-1)`), then run the pass again; a result with no rows means the packs are installed and their files under `dir` removed. A first install takes three passes."},"1710":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-65","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#install_pass","content":"**Errors.** `ErrorCode::InvalidArgument` as for `Store::install`, or for an empty `dir`; the job's own errors are the job's."},"1711":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-66","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#update","content":"Updates the packs (every installed one when empty) to the catalog's releases, keeping the components and languages installed."},"1712":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-67","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#repair","content":"Checks the pack in full and, unless it is whole, fetches what it lacks."},"1713":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-68","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#job","content":"A store's long work on a thread of its own: its progress in bytes, a wait for the next change, a cancel, and its result."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-69","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#job","content":"**Job.** Each language builds its own idioms on these methods: a stream of progress, and the awaited result cancelling the job when the caller's task is cancelled."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-70","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#wait_progress","content":"Waits until the progress moves past `seq` (from `seq`), the job ends, or `timeout_ms` passes; returns the sequence then. Polling with the last one returned sees every change."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-71","page_id":"/docs/reference/store","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/store#wait_progress","content":"**Blocks.** Until the job moves or ends: call it off a UI thread, or use the language's asynchronous form."},"1717":{"id":"/docs/reference/store-72","page_id":"/docs/reference/store"